            <ArticleTitle>CT angiography unmasking catheter-induced spasm as a reason for left main coronary artery stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>406-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jcct.2008.10.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Invasive catheterization can lead to mechanically induced spasm of coronary arteries. In this case report, CT angiography allowed us to unmask catheter-induced coronary spasm as the underlying reason for isolated left main coronary artery stenosis seen in invasive angiography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
